      "problem": "$$\n\nCalculate $\\int \\frac{3}{(2-2{x}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x$ for $|x|>1.$",
      "worked_solution": "$$\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cotangent function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3}{(2-2{x}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{3}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
